Subject: [M154] GPU: apply host-twiddled TexSubImage2D workaround to all
 formats.

The previous use_tex_sub_image_for_host_twiddled_npot_uploads
workaround is needed for more texture formats, so simply apply it to
all formats on affected GPUs, and rename the workaround to
use_tex_sub_image_for_client_data_npot_uploads .

(cherry picked from commit 594bffac95f78e6e73914b494359a3bbb7561826)

Fixed: 561874871
Bug: 559320837
Change-Id: I179c3479bad4bac06cbd1b6465b6f9229178c13d
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8391507
Reviewed-by: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Kenneth Russell <kbr@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Kenneth Russell <kbr@chromium.org>
Cr-Original-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1697432}
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8428580
Bot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com <rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/branch-heads/8037@{#1253}
Cr-Branched-From: e10b20e60f162e7ad88e4930833695a54f4e15fb-refs/heads/main@{#1689415}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
As with the preceding TexSubImage2D workaround pick, this branch's
TextureManager::DoTexSubImage has no `uploaded` flag, so the widened
condition (use_tex_sub_image_for_client_data_npot_uploads, no format
check) was applied to the existing `if (full_image &&
!texture->IsImmutable())` branch rather than the upstream
`if (uploaded) {} else if (...)` form. All other hunks applied as
upstream. No semantic changes.

